-- **WCS axis flip (#1720):** Shipped via `set_wcs_flip` (stored and shown only; the post and generation refuse a flipped WCS by name until the flip is carried into the program).
+- **WCS axis flip (#1720):** Shipped via `set_wcs_flip`. The post carries a flipped X or Y through Fanuc and Haas (#1649). A flipped Z, a flipped and rotated WCS, other posts and operation types outside 3-axis milling are refused by name.
 - **WCS on a circle's centre (#739):** Shipped via `set_wcs_circle_centre` (one edge chain id; the same command as the WCS page's "Circle centre" anchor).
